30,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems our history favors water management over surfacing, and our planting success is... let's say, optimistic at best.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The ground is tricky. Heavy earth-moving is risky due to clay and slippage, and the center of the park is hard to hoard.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, the costs for plants and water are way higher than for paving! And we have so few staff left!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. Our internal staff is depleted. We rely on contractors for turf and water, but we have volunteers for habitats and sports.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The site is a heat trap and the drainage is failing. Also, most people just use it as a thoroughfare to the tram.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, if the drainage is failing and the overflow basin is the only thing that lasted, a water-based solution seems logical.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"But @Benjamin, the firms warned about slippage and clay. A massive reshaping for wetlands might be too risky for the soil.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"But wait! If plants cost triple to maintain and we have no staff, shouldn't we go for something paved and simple?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Paving is cheaper, but we have existing volunteer groups for sports and habitats. We should leverage that free labor.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Paving a heat trap just makes it hotter. We need shade or water, but it must accommodate the tram commuters.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A paved plaza would likely be patched repeatedly, judging by the civic hall apron. I'm leaning away from Option A.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we avoid the center and focus on the south, we can keep the park open. Option D fits the southern location.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,But will the sports terraces be expensive? I'm worried about the long-term budget.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,Sports facilities are often managed by the volunteers Minako mentioned. That reduces the burden on our seven remaining staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"The commuters need firm ground. A woodland walk might be too soft, and wetlands might block the path.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic suggests that if we can't maintain trees and we can't trust paving, we should look at the most durable infrastructure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,Shallow work is cheaper and safer. Option D or A are safer for the soil than Option C.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I just don't want a financial disaster in three years! Paving seems safest for the wallet, but maybe sports are okay?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We have a casual pool for stewarding and volunteers for sports. Option D is the most operationally sustainable.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. It provides firm ground for the tram users and avoids the drainage nightmare of a full wetland.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
